    "result_text": "The build succeeds. The test suite (the single acceptance test, `AcceptanceTest`) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- A single-responsibility step that reads the persisted `Owner` via `@Val` and emits one line to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger (`LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`), containing the owner id, `customerCode` and `registrationDate`.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (`save \u2192 audit \u2192 respond`), under the same `transaction` governance as its neighbours. Placing it after `SaveOwner` guarantees the owner id is assigned, so the audit line only fires on a successful create.\n\nThis follows the project's OfficeFloor conventions \u2014 one small function class with one public method, state passed by `@Val`, wired declaratively in YAML rather than added to an existing step (keeping each step focused). The emitted line, e.g. `AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-16`, contains all three required fields, matching the new acceptance test's assertion.",
